WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.168
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back to

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.202
the captain's quarters.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.371
After today,
we sadly have just

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.974
three shows remaining before
returning to the studio,

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:10.744
and yet, so many plot lines
we haven't gotten to.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.745
For example there's bee plot

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.114
with the giant ghost lobster
we promised you.

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:19.652
-My agent told me this would be
a multi-episode arc.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.855
-We were gonna have an
intervention for Steve,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.923
the fish, who probably has a
drug problem.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.958
-My only problem is
I like to party.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:29.362
-And Ira the Prospect Park duck
requested we do a full

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.432
"Closer Look" about
water fowl education.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.967
-Well, because we have
nine ducklings

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.134
and we need to know
what the deal is

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:36.569
with school in the fall,
you know.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.572
Like, is it remote?
Is it a combo?

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.208
Hey, Seth, do you know what
ducks use instead of iPads?

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:45.044
-What's that, Ira?
-Lily pads. [ Laughs ]

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.879
-Oh, boy!
-Oh, okay.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.882
So Ira can't make jokes.
Good to know. Very helpful.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:52.519
-Also our beloved Sea Captain
is celebrating the results

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.487
of last week's poll,
where we asked,

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:57.289
"Do you enjoy the Sea Captain
during this difficult time?

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.092
And "Yes, he's a nice addition"

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.361
beat "No, I hate fun."
in a landslide.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:05.097
Now, this time there was not a
third option called "Other."

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:07.367
But a lot of you have asked,
what would've happened

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.302
if there had been,
and if,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.070
in that scenario,
"Other" has won.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.271
Well, in that case,

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.140
we would've introduced
a new character

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.543
the sexy mermaid,
with the un-sexy voice.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:20.679
-Well, hello there.
-Very pleased to meet you.

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:23.283
-Hi, hot stuff.
-Any of you fellas

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.185
wanna take a dip?
-Uhh.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:28.087
-No thank you.
-Um, I'm okay.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.090
Don't love the water.
-And speaking of bummers...

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.459
-Lazy segue.
-President Trump

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.861
and the Republican Party are in
lockstep behind the plan

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.598
to dismantle the Post Office
that is both an assault

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.034
on democracy and the culmination
of a decades-long movement

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:44.203
to privatize one of the
country's most cherished

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.504
public institutions.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.774
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.811
♪♪

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.513
House Democrats announced
yesterday

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.782
that they'll be returning from
recess early to address

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:59.352
the crisis at the Post Office,
after it was reported

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:02.021
that mail sorting machines,
across the country,

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.824
were being removed and the
Postal Service had warned

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.360
46 states
that voters could be

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.329
disenfranchised
due to the changes.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.830
And if you're wondering,
if it's just coincidental

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.799
that the Post Office
is being dismantled

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.202
as the country nears an election
that will depend

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.371
in large part
on mail-in voting,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.006
one, congrats on waking up
from your coma.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:23.709
And two, here's Trump admitting
it last week.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:28.348
-They want $25 billion,
billion, for the Post Office.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.883
Now, they need that money in
order to have the Post Office

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.352
work so it can take all of these
millions and millions

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.854
of ballots, and if they don't
get those two items,

00:02:35.854 --> 00:02:39.024
that means that you can't have
universal mail-in voting.

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:41.360
-Once again,
he just confesses.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.462
Just like he did with
Russian hacking

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.030
and the Ukraine quid pro quo.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.801
he confesses like he has James
Bond strapped to a table.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.469
[ As Trump ] You're prbably
wondering how I'm gonna steal

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:54.273
the election, well I'll tell you
every detail, Mr. Bond.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.842
And then I'll turn the laser on
and leave the room.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.444
-[ Normal voice ] The entire
Trump presidency has been

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.746
like an episode
of "Law and Order"

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.982
where the killer confesses
in the first five minutes

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.951
and then they turn it over to a
cable news panel to discuss.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:07.386
I mean, sure
he said he killed him

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:08.854
and then where
he buried the body

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.890
and when they dug up the body
it did have traces of his DNA,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.026
but can we really, can we really
take him at his word?

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:17.730
Or are we maybe over [As Trump]
Are we maybe over-reacting?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.332
[ Normal voice ] Now, as we
and many others have stated,

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:23.402
millions of times,
there is zero evidence

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:26.238
of widespread fraud
in mail-in voting.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.074
Even Trump's own voting
integrity commission

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.742
couldn't find any evidence
of voter fraud.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.611
In fact, if anything,
mail-in voting is especially

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:35.581
secure, because you have the
physical evidence.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:38.117
If you suspect fraud, you just
look at the name and signature

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.420
on the ballot and make sure it's
a legal vote.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.855
And yet on Sunday,
Trump's Chief of Staff,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.757
Mark Meadows,
kept repeating the lie

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.159
that mail-in voting could
somehow lead to fraud.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.561
-You don't call up and say --

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.063
-There's no evidence of
wide-spread voter fraud though.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:54.433
But there's no evidence of
widespread voter fraud.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:56.468
-There's no, there's no,
there's no evidence

00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:58.838
that there's not either.
-That's not how evidence works.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:02.141
You can't arrest someone
for possession of cocaine

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.810
because they can't prove they
don't have any cocaine.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.580
&gt;&gt; [ Laughs ]
But do you have any?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.683
-I can get some,
if you join me for a dip.

00:04:11.683 --> 00:04:15.921
-[ Groans ] No thanks,
I'm going to get clean.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:18.924
-[ Whispers ] That was the
intervention.

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.526
-I just had that same
Meadows argument

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.761
with my 4-year-old son.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.262
There's not a monster
in your closet.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:25.264
[ As son ] There's no evidence,
there isn't either.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.565
[ Normal voice ]
Damn it, you got me.

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:28.800
Where did you learn
the Meadows Maneuver, boy?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.370
[ As son ]
You have CNN on all day.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.572
I learned it from you, dad.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.540
[ Normal voice ] Now, even
before Donald Trump's

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.409
rise to power, there was a
decade's-long effort

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:40.679
by right wing billionaires
and dead eyed corporate husks

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.748
To privatize the Post Office
which is,

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:45.418
According to many polls,
the single most popular

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.052
public institution in
America.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:49.488
And if you don't believe me,
just watch this ad

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:52.424
from Massachusetts Senator
Ed Markey featuring some of

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:56.429
the most likable Boston postal
workers you will ever see.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:59.232
-The Postal Service handles
in one day

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:03.368
more business than FedEx
and UPS do in a year.

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:06.738
It's an integral part
of the economy of this country

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:08.707
and the security
of this country.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:12.178
And right now, it's an important
part of democracy.

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:15.080
We're in every town,
we delivered to every house

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.617
every day, the infrastructures,
it can't be matched.

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:21.120
If they privatize this
institution,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.122
we'll be at the mercy
of corporations

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.891
and we all know
they have no mercy.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.427
-So great that masks can
keep out coronavirus

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:31.397
but are completely impervious to
a Boston accent.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.298
No one who was watching that
thinking:

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:34.767
"Where are those
gentleman from?"

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.135
[ Boston accent ] Hey, we're
shooting a commercial.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.704
Can somebody quiet the [ Bleep ]
Seagulls down?

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.239
[ Normal voice ] How can you
not love those guys?

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.908
It's like if the Post Office
was directed by Ben Affleck.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:46.779
[ As Affleck ] We service more
homes in a day than FedEx, UPS,

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:50.115
and we are sorry to say,
even your mother.

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:51.384
[ Normal voice ] Post Office has
been woven into

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.285
the fabric of America since
before the founding.

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:55.120
It's as old as
the Republic itself.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.489
It's literally
in the Constitution.

00:05:57.489 --> 00:05:59.658
-U.S. Postal Service has been
delivering mail

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:01.594
since before
the Declaration of Independence

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.029
was even signed.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.765
President George Washington
signed the Postal Service Act

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:09.034
which authorized Congress to
create the U.S. Postal Service.

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:11.203
This established routes
and made it illegal

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:12.771
to open anyone's mail.

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.407
-That's right,
George Washington

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.643
made it illegal to
open anyone else's mail.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:20.112
Of course, Washington couldn't
have envisioned living in

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.648
a New York City apartment
and getting mail for the

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:24.417
previous five tenants every day.

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.952
By the way, if you're watching
Melvin Schwartz,

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:28.254
Rebecca had the baby,
and yet,

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:30.690
despite its storied
place in our history,

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.459
there's long been an effort by
Republicans and billionaires

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.694
like Charles Koch
to privatize it,

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:39.132
as far back as 1988,
Ronald Reagan's budget director

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:41.734
James Miller said
there's no good reason

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.435
why the Postal Service
should remain

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:46.539
part of the U.S. government
and no good reason why it should

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:49.341
enjoy a monopoly over the
delivery of letter mail.

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.944
Yeah, why would you want to
stick a 55 cent stamp

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.846
on your letter when you could
walk to the FedEx store

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.981
and wait in line to pay $12
for the same service,

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:58.417
and while we're at it, why
should the interior department

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:00.319
have a monopoly on the parks?

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.421
Let's sell the naming rights to
some private companies

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:05.491
and turn it into Yellow Cold
Stone Creamery National Park

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.459
or Mountain Dew Code Redwood
National Park.

00:07:07.459 --> 00:07:10.029
We could replace Smokey Bear
with a corporate mascot

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.832
like Chester Cheetah
or the Taco Bell Chihuahua.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:14.000
<i> Yo quiero forest fires.</i>

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.135
Incidentally,
that Reagan official Miller

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:18.070
later went on to serve on the
Postal Service

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.872
Board of Governors until his
nomination was

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:22.408
thankfully blocked
by Senator Bernie Sanders

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.576
at the behest
of the Postal Unions

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:26.212
and you know
Bernie loves mail.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:28.680
It's like one of those guys who
waits for the mail carrier

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.616
on the stoop every morning
and knows more

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:31.784
about their route
than they do.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:32.919
[ As Bernie ]
Morning, Shirley.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.787
Got those CB2 catalogs today,
right?

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:36.021
And be careful on fourth avenue.

00:07:36.021 --> 00:07:37.456
There's a new puddle.

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:38.824
[ Normal voice ] And on Sunday,
Bernie was one of the most

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:41.494
vocal Democrats calling
for an immediate investigation

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.929
of the changes at the USPS.

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:46.799
-Do you think Speaker Pelosi
should call

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:51.937
the House of Representatives
back to get a free-standing bill

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:55.474
to fund the Post Office
to the Senate

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:59.144
and then to the president and do
you think that

00:07:59.144 --> 00:08:03.649
the House of Representatives
should be using

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:06.352
their oversight role
and investigating what exactly

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:08.220
is going on in terms of
the changes

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.690
that the postmaster general
is making?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.428
-The answer to both questions
is yes.

00:08:15.428 --> 00:08:18.698
Over three months ago,
three months ago,

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:21.967
Democrats in the House passed
the Heroes Bill,

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:27.873
and among many other things,
it provided $25 billion

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:29.675
for the Postal Service.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:32.111
Bernie's so committed to
protecting the Postal Service,

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:35.447
he called in on a Sunday
from his weekend home

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:38.984
inside an "Avatar" movie?

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:42.054
Seriously, Bernie, what in the
world is this Zoom background?

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:45.891
It looks like the default screen
saver on Windows 95.

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:48.794
Surprised he's not surrounded
by flying toasters.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.395
This is why you got to love
Bernie.

00:08:50.395 --> 00:08:53.398
The president is a cheesy crook
doing press conferences

00:08:53.398 --> 00:08:55.768
at his ritzy golf clubs
for his millionaire buddies

00:08:55.768 --> 00:08:58.671
and Bernie looks like he's on
the cover of a "Sleep Sounds"

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:00.506
album from 1985.

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:02.174
[ As Bernie ] Listen to the
sounds of the forest,

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:04.976
the birds chirping,
the creek running.

00:09:04.976 --> 00:09:07.412
Go to sleep already, come on,
I've got things to do.

00:09:07.412 --> 00:09:08.613
-[ Normal voice ] So, in many
ways what we're seeing

00:09:08.613 --> 00:09:10.115
is not new,
it's been a goal

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.783
of the conservative
movement for years.

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:13.752
They want to turn one of
America's cherished

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.721
public institutions
into a chain restaurant

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:17.189
where you can buy
a pack of stamps

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:18.557
and unlimited bread sticks.

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:21.093
Privatizing the Post Office
is like turning your local

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:23.462
fire station
into the cable company.

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:24.930
My house is on fire.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.298
We'll be there between 9:00
and 1:00.

00:09:26.298 --> 00:09:28.768
Make sure someone is home.

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:30.936
And yet,
as an election approaches

00:09:30.936 --> 00:09:33.372
in which the incumbent President
just happens to be

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.841
trailing badly in the polls,
conservatives are suddenly

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:38.377
concerned that
the Post Office loses money.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:41.313
Former FOX Business host
Trish Reagan captured

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:43.082
this sentiment yesterday
when she tweeted,

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:45.217
"Here's the deal on the
United States Postal Service.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:46.385
It's just a bad business!

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.354
Poorly run loses billions.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:51.123
If it were any other business,
it would have gone under by now.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:52.724
We need to make it more
accountable,

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:54.827
not keep throwing money at it."

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:57.229
Yeah, but it's not a business.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:59.865
So telling that you ghouls never
say stuff like this

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:01.600
about I.C.E. or the police.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.069
The Pentagon's more flops than
Johnny Depp but you guys

00:10:04.069 --> 00:10:05.538
still love
to throw money at it.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:07.072
Also,
as we explained last week,

00:10:07.072 --> 00:10:09.375
the Post Office was actually
profitable until Republicans

00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:13.545
passed a law in 2006 requiring
it to pre-fund 75 years

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.548
of retiree health benefits
in ten years

00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:17.983
and without that law,
the Post Office would have

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:19.284
remained profitable.

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:21.353
-It operated at a loss
in the first couple of years

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:23.789
in the 21st century,
but by 2003,

00:10:23.789 --> 00:10:25.791
it was back to operating
out of profit.

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:29.762
In fact, from 2003 through 2006,
USPS recorded

00:10:29.762 --> 00:10:32.731
a total $9.3 billion profit.

00:10:32.731 --> 00:10:35.768
If not for the 75 year pension
in health care obligation,

00:10:35.768 --> 00:10:37.936
the USPS would have recorded
operating profits

00:10:37.936 --> 00:10:39.371
for the last six years.

00:10:39.371 --> 00:10:41.173
-The Post Office
turned a profit.

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:42.474
Even Uber isn't profitable.

00:10:42.474 --> 00:10:44.809
In fact, if anything,
Uber should be taking cues

00:10:44.809 --> 00:10:47.313
from the Postal Service instead
of their Chevy Suburban,

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.981
they should be riding around
picking people up

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:50.282
in a mail truck.

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.684
Hang tight, I've got to pick up
three more people.

00:10:51.684 --> 00:10:54.052
So the same Republicans who are
now complaining

00:10:54.052 --> 00:10:57.456
that the Post Office loses money
are the ones responsible for

00:10:57.456 --> 00:10:59.091
the Post Office losing money.

00:10:59.091 --> 00:11:00.960
Like if your boss
at Krispy Kreme says,

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.161
"Why is no one
coming to the store?"

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.095
And you said,
"You made us put up that sign

00:11:04.095 --> 00:11:06.031
that said we stick our [Bleep]
In all the crullers."

00:11:06.031 --> 00:11:07.700
Also, side note,
is there anything

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.401
George W. Bush
didn't make worse?

00:11:09.401 --> 00:11:12.004
The guy wrecked everything
from the Middle East to the mail

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.839
to a bunch of
perfectly good canvasses.

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:16.275
I know some people have a
tendency to gloss over

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:18.544
his eight years as President
but next time you get

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:20.980
a wedding invitation in the mail
six months after the wedding,

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.115
just remember,
mission uncomplished.

00:11:23.115 --> 00:11:26.318
and now the privatizers have
joined forces with the president

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:29.021
who's desperate to subvert
an election he knows

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:31.824
he can't win fairly,
which is why he's installed

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:34.526
the Postmaster General
Louis DeJoy with tens

00:11:34.526 --> 00:11:38.129
of millions of dollars worth of
conflicts who donated $360,000

00:11:38.129 --> 00:11:40.900
to Trump and the RNC,
which is unprecedented.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.201
The Post Office is supposed to
be non-partisan.

00:11:43.201 --> 00:11:45.737
Putting this guy in charge of
the Post Office is like putting

00:11:45.737 --> 00:11:47.473
Tom Selleck in charge of "HUD."

00:11:47.473 --> 00:11:49.442
Don't worry,
I won't take your house.

00:11:49.442 --> 00:11:51.676
Would "Mr. Baseball" lie to you?

00:11:51.676 --> 00:11:53.912
DeJoy has been gutting
the Post Office just as

00:11:53.912 --> 00:11:56.214
states prepare for a surge
in mail-in ballots,

00:11:56.214 --> 00:11:59.184
thanks to the deadly plague
Trump failed to stop.

00:11:59.184 --> 00:12:01.920
He slowed mail delivery,
slashed hours at Post Offices,

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.356
removed mail sorting machines
across the country,

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:07.927
and told 46 states their voters
could be disenfranchised

00:12:07.927 --> 00:12:09.761
by delayed mail-in ballots
and by the way,

00:12:09.761 --> 00:12:11.429
it's not a matter of whether
the Postal Service

00:12:11.429 --> 00:12:12.931
can handle the volume.

00:12:12.931 --> 00:12:15.667
Even if every single one of the
150 million registered voters

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:17.903
mailed in a ballot, that would
be nothing compared to

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:19.671
the Post Office's usual load.

00:12:19.671 --> 00:12:22.341
The Postal Service processes
nearly 500 million

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:25.344
pieces of mail every day
and it annually handles

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:28.447
more than 3 billion pieces in
the week before Christmas alone.

00:12:28.447 --> 00:12:30.248
Yeah, and just think of
how crucial that

00:12:30.248 --> 00:12:31.517
week before Christmas is.

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:33.919
We've all had that moment
of terror where we realize

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:35.487
we forgot to get a gift
for a loved one,

00:12:35.487 --> 00:12:37.355
panic bought something
at the last minute,

00:12:37.355 --> 00:12:39.291
chose overnight shipping
and then wrapped it

00:12:39.291 --> 00:12:40.459
in old newspaper.

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:42.360
Here you go, honey,
remember when you said

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.029
we needed a new
toilet brush?

00:12:44.029 --> 00:12:46.564
Well, I remembered.

00:12:46.564 --> 00:12:48.500
What we're witnessing right now
is a marriage

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.503
of Postal Service privatizers
and an anti-majoritarian

00:12:51.503 --> 00:12:53.973
political movement intent on
undermining democracy

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:56.642
in order to impose its will
on everyone else.

00:12:56.642 --> 00:12:58.110
They know they can't win fairly,

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.411
so they'll do anything
to cheat,

00:12:59.411 --> 00:13:01.646
including dismantling
one of our most cherished

00:13:01.646 --> 00:13:04.717
public institutions because --
-They have no mercy.

00:13:04.717 --> 00:13:06.852
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

